   191	& \paraphraseControlCount{} \\
   192	Closed book
   193	& \closedBookAccuracy{} [\closedBookAccuracyLow{}, \closedBookAccuracyHigh{}]
   194	& \closedBookCount{} \\
   195	\bottomrule
   196	\end{tabular}
   197	}
   198	\end{table}
   199	
   200	Removing only the retained decoy raised accuracy to \pruningNoDecoyAccuracy{}\%. This change was \pruningNoDecoyChange{} points [\pruningNoDecoyChangeLow{}, \pruningNoDecoyChangeHigh{}], with \pruningNoDecoyWins{} wins and no losses. Literal wording changed matched accuracy by \literalControlChange{} points, with \literalControlWins{} wins and no losses. Across all outputs, distractor capture was \distractorCaptureRate{}\%, exact-output compliance was \exactOutputComplianceRate{}\%, and invalid output was \invalidOutputRate{}\%. These diagnostics identify selection of the retained lexical competitor, rather than answer deletion, as the failure in this grid. They do not establish how another pruning rule would behave.
   201	
   202	\section{Limitations}
   203	
   204	The findings concern one small quantized model and may not transfer to larger models or other quantization levels. Synthetic clause lookup is not natural contract analysis, and retrieval accuracy is not a measure of general capability. The \cpuBudgetMinutes{}-minute CPU budget capped the grid, leaving only \tierEightCount{} full-context probes at the longest tier and wide intervals throughout. That sparse tier prevents a conclusion about degradation within the measured range, and the experiment cannot address longer prompts. The filler comparison confounds topical relation with semantic domain, entity and code density, candidate count, and sentence templates. A factorial design that matches those properties would be needed to identify a topical-relevance effect. Greedy decoding removes run-to-run sampling variation but does not show how sampling would change the estimates. The mitigation is a deliberately simple keyword filter, and its decoy-removal control depends on an oracle label unavailable in natural documents.
   205	
   206	\section{Reproducibility}
   207	
   208	Analysis scripts generate every reported quantity from the committed probe manifest and raw model outputs. This procedure follows the principle that reports of computational evidence should expose their budget and variation \citep{dodge2019show}. The model and cached data are frozen and checksummed, and each raw output retains its stable probe identifier. Running \texttt{make all} regenerates \texttt{results.json}, the LaTeX value macros, and the paper from cached outputs; running \texttt{make clean-deep \&\& make all} repeats deterministic model inference. Repository gates check frozen inputs, citation resolution, number provenance, pipeline freshness, result sanity, prose style, anonymity, and compilation.
   209	
   210	\label{main-body-end}
   211	\bibliography{refs}
   212	\bibliographystyle{icml2026}
   213	
   214	\end{document}

