 \section{Limitations}
 
-The findings concern one small quantized model and may not transfer to larger models or other quantization levels. Synthetic clause lookup is not natural contract analysis, and retrieval accuracy is not a measure of general capability. The \cpuBudgetMinutes{}-minute CPU budget capped the grid, leaving only \tierEightCount{} full-context probes at the longest tier and wide intervals throughout. That sparse tier prevents a conclusion about degradation within the measured range, and the experiment cannot address longer prompts. The filler comparison confounds topical relation with semantic domain, entity and code density, candidate count, and sentence templates. A factorial design that matches those properties would be needed to identify a topical-relevance effect. Greedy decoding removes run-to-run sampling variation but does not show how sampling would change the estimates. The mitigation is a deliberately simple keyword filter, and its decoy-removal control depends on an oracle label unavailable in natural documents.
+The findings concern one small quantized model and may not transfer to larger models or other quantization levels. Synthetic clause lookup is not natural contract analysis, and retrieval accuracy is not a measure of general capability. The \cpuBudgetMinutes{}-minute CPU budget capped the grid, leaving only \tierEightCount{} full-context probes at the longest tier and wide intervals throughout. That sparse tier prevents a conclusion about degradation within the measured range, and the experiment cannot address longer prompts. The filler comparison confounds topical relation with semantic domain, entity and code density, candidate count, and sentence templates. A factorial design that matches those properties would be needed to identify a topical-relevance effect. Greedy decoding removes run-to-run sampling variation but does not show how sampling would change the estimates. Query-entity selection assumes that the question names one company exactly and that the relevant sentence repeats that name. It does not address aliases, pronouns, or queries without a unique named subject. The decoy-removal control also depends on an oracle label unavailable in natural documents.
 
